{
  "id": "cognitive-miser",
  "term": "cognitive miser",
  "definition": "Cognitive miser refers to the idea that people often rely on mental shortcuts, such as trust, credibility judgments, and perceptions of risks or benefits, instead of detailed knowledge when forming opinions or support. In this view, immediate judgments are shaped more by heuristics than by what a person objectively knows.",
